    "description": "US nationals are third-country nationals for Dutch immigration. The standard route for salaried employment is the Highly Skilled Migrant (kennismigrant) residence permit, sponsored by an IND-recognised employer; the EU Blue Card is an alternative for higher-salaried graduates. US nationals are MVV-exempt (no entry visa). After arrival the employee collects the residence permit from the IND, registers at the municipality (gemeente / BRP) to obtain a BSN, and takes out Dutch health insurance. REPRESENTATIVE — confirm with the IND."
  },
